-- title:
--   Injectivity of substitution detected on residue fields
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative Noetherian ring and let $\varphi = (\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$ be a pair of power series in two variables over $B$, i.e. an element of `Series B` $= \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to B[[X_0,X_1]]$, each of whose members has vanishing constant coefficient. Assume that the quotient `FormalODModule.KerAlgebra` $\varphi = B[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$, the quotient by the ideal generated by the range of $\varphi$, is a finite $B$-module. Assume further the residue-field hypothesis: for every field $\kappa$ (in the same universe as $B$) and every surjective ring homomorphism $g : B \to \kappa$ such that $\kappa[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varphi_0^{g},\varphi_1^{g})$ is a finite-dimensional $\kappa$-vector space, where $\varphi^{g}$ denotes the coefficientwise image `Series.map g φ`, substitution of $\varphi^{g}$ is injective on $\kappa[[X_0,X_1]]$, i.e. $f' \mapsto f'(\varphi_0^{g},\varphi_1^{g})$ is injective. Then for all $f, g \in B[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $\mathrm{subst}\,\varphi\,f = \mathrm{subst}\,\varphi\,g$ one has $f = g$; that is, substitution along $\varphi$ is injective on $B[[X_0,X_1]]$.
--
--   This is a descent statement for injectivity of substitution along a pair of variable-free power series: over a Noetherian base with finite quotient algebra, injectivity of substitution may be checked after reduction to the residue fields of $B$. It is used in the analysis of kernels of isogenies of formal modules, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_X_pow_mem_span_of_X_pow_mem_span_comp`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_X_pow_mem_span_of_X_pow_mem_span_comp) and by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.subst_injective_of_hasKernelOfDegree`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.subst_injective_of_hasKernelOfDegree).
-- source:
